From c575db8f98e6c4f65f9a5c324c419af85a87d86d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 05:13:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Peters family memorials + John Peters as homepage showcase
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three new memorials — Samuel, Ruth and James Peters — written from
existing canon (GlenTab markers, TreeTab relations, John's life story).
Marked `unlisted`: full pages by slug, but kept out of the public
/memorials directory since they belong to the John Peters demo.

- GlenTab: every grave with a memorial now links to it. John still
  switches tabs in-page; the other three navigate to their pages.
- TreeTab: deceased members link through to their memorials. Living
  members deliberately do not — no page exists and consent rules apply.
- Home: John Peters demo leads, followed immediately by the five-tab
  teaser so every room is one scroll from the top. The large Founding
  Memorial section (Virginia's portrait) is removed from the homepage.
- Footer: quiet permanent credit, 'Inspired by Virginia Dadirayi
  Chiimba — Founding Memorial', linking to her memorial.

All five tabs retained, including Living Legacy. Family Glen keeps its
name. Virginia's and John's memorial pages are untouched.
